# My Reading Log

## Strange Pictures — *Uketsu*
**Rating:** ★★★★ (4/5)
**Read:** Apr 26
**Genres:** Mystery

*Woman kills her mother, husband and daughter in law*

I enjoy a good whodunnit. But this felt more like withholding information rather than discovering it. And I felt the way they tied everything together at the end was a tad convenient. Overall still an enjoyable read.

## Head Above Water — *CE Ricci*
**Rating:** ★★★.5 (3.5/5)
**Read:** Mar 26
**Genres:** MM

*Step brothers reunite after their parents’ death*

The brothers thing kinda nagged me in the back of my mind. And I don’t know how I feel about having sex at your parents’ funeral. It was a little too dramatic, with the bottom having a full on breakdown most of the book. But I enjoyed the spice. The vocab did get a bit repetitive but I guess there’s only so many ways to say erection. 

## The Long Game — *Rachel Reid*
**Rating:** ★★★★★ (5/5)
**Read:** Mar 26
**Genres:** MM

*Charity, therapy and marriage*

I can see why this is the highest rated book in the series. I was worried it would get boring now that they’re together, but Reid still serves up that juicy tension. This book leans towards ilya’s POV, and his struggle with mental illness, which is relatable. Shane’s obliviousness is cute and frustrating, which is also relatable. The issues don’t exactly get resolved by the end, but it rarely does in real life either. Fodder for the next book I guess. Can’t wait!

